WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.560
- I sometimes fantasize about Splinter,

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.393
he's Asian.

00:00:02.393 --> 00:00:03.397
- He's a rat.

00:00:03.397 --> 00:00:04.230
- He's a good father.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.813
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.957 --> 00:00:11.310
- "Bridesmaids" is an absolute
classic, "Girl's Trip."

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.710
You know, those films
really inspired this film

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.750
in the sense of debauchery,

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.371
unapologetic, in your face,

00:00:18.371 --> 00:00:19.770
and like, you know,
breaking out of these boxes

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.120
that society has put us in.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.700
- You know, I love
"Bruce Almighty" so much.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.870
It makes me weep.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:28.500
You know, I do love the
Austin Powers series.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.090
Yeah, true millennial, yeah.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.890
Don't ask Sabrina, because they're cuspy.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.500
They're like, "Austin what?"

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.333
Children.

00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:36.510
- Of course "Bridesmaids",

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.830
that's really one that,

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.060
it felt like it broke the mold.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.047
It was like, it was at a
time where people were like,

00:00:41.047 --> 00:00:42.600
"Are women funny?"

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.160
And it's like, yeah we are,

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.470
and it really felt like
it helped the cause

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.710
in terms of us being here on
the backs of movies like that.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:52.380
- And I always like to take
it way back to "American Pie".

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.690
That was a movie that when
I saw this R-rated comedy,

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.490
it was a thing where I
saw it and then literally

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:58.350
24 hours later I got a bunch of my friends

00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.490
to also go see it.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.860
That's what we hope happens
with this movie as well,

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.500
and it really is so much more
fun to see a movie like this

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.820
in a theater with a bunch of friends,

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.410
with hundreds of people at once.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:11.430
- I literally love "Bridesmaids"
and I love "Pitch Perfect".

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.367
Love "Girls Trip".

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:15.120
"Pitch Perfect" has a
special place in my heart

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.440
because when it came out,

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.390
I liked the movie so
much I literally thought

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.860
if I taught myself how to beatbox I could

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.530
maybe play the sibling
of the Asian beatboxer

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:25.876
in the first one in
sequels, and now here I am.

00:01:25.876 --> 00:01:28.081
- I hate myself because the
first thing that I though of was

00:01:28.081 --> 00:01:30.420
"Crazy Rich Asians" and
that's just like gross.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.430
I mean comedy, "American Pie".

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.620
I saw Seth Rogen before, so
all the Seth Rogen movies

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.453
are on my mind.

00:01:35.453 --> 00:01:36.330
I do enjoy comedies.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.400
I like switching off into
something to laugh, so,

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.360
that's what we're doing tonight.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.240
- I love Mel Brooks movies
and I love the Cohen brothers.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:43.897
Those are kind of the funniest to me ever.

00:01:43.897 --> 00:01:46.860
- "Pineapple Express" one
of my favorites, "Superbad".

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.957
Jackie Chan was a huge influence
in the beginning for me.

00:01:49.957 --> 00:01:51.937
"Shanghai Noon", "Shanghai Nights",

00:01:51.937 --> 00:01:53.077
"80 Days Around the World".

00:01:53.077 --> 00:01:57.210
- "Midnight Run" is my, like,
favorite all time comedy.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:59.160
I'm gonna stick with that
one. That's my movie.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.230
- All of the "Fletch" movies,
which don't necessarily

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:03.120
age that well, but there
are still things about them

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.897
that are like, the timing is great.

00:02:04.897 --> 00:02:06.690
"The Hangover", "Bringing Up Baby",

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.460
and "The Philadelphia Story".

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.897
- I grew up watching a lot
of comedies with my dad.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:13.567
"The Breakfast Club", "Stripes", "Fletch",

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:17.070
"Caddyshack", "Overboard"
with Goldie Hawn.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.507
Anything with Madeline Kahn.

00:02:19.507 --> 00:02:21.690
"Young Frankenstein's"
one of my favorites.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:24.180
Mel Brooks. "History of the World".

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.833
I miss those movies.

